% The third route to elevating legrests: a manual fully reclining back
% (E1226, claim 3) that meets its own criteria on the same base. The reviewer
% finds no cast, brace or edema, so the legrests rest on the reclining back
% alone (an open finding would add a conditional answer beside this one).
scenario legrests_with_reclining_back is:
    claim 1 is for the legrests.
    the HCPCS code of the legrests is "K0195".
    the legrests is an accessory of the power wheelchair.
    the legrests is furnished to Ann.
    the finding elevating legrests needed about Ann is unsupported, according to the reviewer, because "the record documents neither a cast or brace limiting knee flexion nor edema of the lower extremities".
    claim 3 is for the reclining back.
    the HCPCS code of the reclining back is "E1226".
    the reclining back is an accessory of the power wheelchair.
    the reclining back is furnished to Ann.
    the finding manual reclining back needed about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "intermittent catheterization for bladder management and unable to independently transfer from the wheelchair to the bed".
    claim 2 is for the power wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the power wheelchair is "K0823".
    the power wheelchair is furnished to Ann.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair not self propellable about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding scooter ruled out about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding power wheelchair can be safely operated about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates power wheelchair about Ann is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding power wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use power wheelchair at home about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Ann is 180 pounds.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary"].

